Subject: [PATCH 02/12] R80b, part 2, patch 2 (cld-advisor, at main's word in
 M14; Review 80, a reader's finding F2, checked by main with a plant of its
 own that passes): THE SCRIPT'S CHECK FUNCTION IS CALLED, AND MUST RECORD A
 FALSE THING AS FAILING.

WHAT STOOD. Main's plant gives the script's own function for a check a signature under which it ignores what it is passed. Every check then reads as holding. The lock passed.

WHAT IS CHANGED. A test loads the script's definitions, calls the function with a false thing and with a true thing, and asks that the result, the table of results, the list of failures and the printed line each say so.

THE PLANTED CASES, in the patch's own test: main's plant and two more ways to the same end (the result typed as holding; the printed line typed as ok). The function of each planted script is called and is reported. The digest of the patch before this one sees the same changes; this sees what they do.

The lock: 17 tests pass. 0 of 19.
